                <tr id="issuerow12542500" rel="12542500" data-issuekey="CXF-4106" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-4106" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-4106">CXF-4106</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Attachments get lost when WSDL claims HTTP transport but config uses JMS
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jens Granseuer
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jens Granseuer
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 14/Feb/12 09:24 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Apr/12 16:45 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 21/Mar/12 21:51 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.5.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.5.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m trying to call a service that claims SOAP with Attachments via an HTTP transport. In reality, however, the service is connected via JMS, so I&#39;m overwriting the transportId in the Spring config. In the request that is sent out from the client the attachment is missing. Instead, it is included as a second XML element in the SOAP body.<br/>
<br/>
According to Dan, this is because the change in transport resets a couple of things to defaults, see http://cxf.547215.n5.nabble.com/SOAP-w-Attachments-still-supported-td5454220.htm
  </td>
