                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Linux CentOS 6
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The call to UriInfo.getHost() is caching the first request&#39;s host and always returning that on all subsequent calls.<br/>
<br/>
For example, Tomcat starts up and a request is made to the server using a URL of &quot;http://1.2.3.4/apicall&quot;, getHost() returns &quot;1.2.3.4&quot;, the next request is made using a URL of &quot;http://mydomainname.com/apicall&quot;, getHost() still returns &quot;1.2.3.4&quot;, where &quot;mydomainname.com&quot; is expected.<br/>

  </td>
