                <tr id="issuerow12542875" rel="12542875" data-issuekey="CXF-4116" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-4116" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-4116">CXF-4116</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Equal URI templates should use a string comparison as the last step
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 16/Feb/12 15:52 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Apr/12 16:45 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 16/Feb/12 16:42 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.4.7,                     2.5.3,                     2.6            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      JAX-RS 1.1 Selection algorithm does not say what needs to be done when 2 URI templates are equal after 3 checks (number of 1. literals, 2. vars &amp; 3. custom vars) are done. CXF assumes both are equal candidates, Jersey finishes with the string comparison. <br/>
<br/>
Note, this 4th step (string comparison) does not make sense in all but few cases where only custom regular expressions are involved due to the fact that steps 1-3 are sufficient in most cases and when it needs to be done we are at the stage where the choice between 2 candidates is completely random... For the interop &amp; portability purposes, it makes sense to add a string comparison...JAX-RS 2.0 requesting the clarification in the spec is to be created too.
  </td>
