                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If we want to publish a CXF service which WSDL is get by using http://xxx , we can not configure the http conduit timeout just by using http-conf:conduit element in the Spring configuration file.<br/>
After digging the code for a while, I found the HttpConduit which is created by the TransportURIResolver has a beanName with null. That could explain why the http-conf:conduit configuration can not be picked up.
