                <tr id="issuerow12551748" rel="12551748" data-issuekey="CXF-4252" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-4252" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-4252">CXF-4252</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                cxf:list-endpoints karaf command should also have a busid column
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Freeman Fang
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Freeman Fang
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Freeman Fang
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 20/Apr/12 08:55 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 05/Jun/12 13:31 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 23/Apr/12 04:17 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.5.4,                     2.6.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The cxf:start-endpoint and cxf:stop-endpoint commands take a bus name and an endpoint name as arguments. But when you list the endpoints using cxf:list-endpoints, the listing only gives the endpoint name. So, you kind of have to guess the bus name when invoking cxf:start-endpoint or cxf:stop-endpoint. It would be easier if the cxf:list-endpoints command also had a column to show the bus name
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
