                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      As you know CXF management provides a lots MBeans out of box. It works perfect if it run as stand alone.<br/>
If we deploy the CXF endpoints into container like Apache Karaf, we may hit the issue that Object is already registered. That is because we don&#39;t build up unique Object name for JMX to use.<br/>
<br/>
To resolve this issue I suggest we add the &quot;instance.id&quot; on the ObjectName. As JMX supports to look up the object with a query string, I don&#39;t think this change will effect much on the user CXF management codes.<br/>

  </td>
