</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Apache Maven 3.0.4 (r1232337; 2012-01-17 03:44:56-0500)<br/>
Maven home: C:\Java\apache-maven-3.0.4\bin\..<br/>
Java version: 1.6.0_31, vendor: Sun Microsystems Inc.<br/>
Java home: C:\Program Files\Java\jdk1.6.0_31\jre<br/>
Default locale: en_US, platform encoding: Cp1252<br/>
OS name: &quot;windows 7&quot;, version: &quot;6.1&quot;, arch: &quot;amd64&quot;, family: &quot;windows&quot;
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When our users mistakenly send non-SOAP XML to our server embedding CXF, they get this unhelpful error:<br/>
<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
No namespace on &quot;{0}&quot; element.<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
<br/>
Where \{0\} is the root element.<br/>
<br/>
The following would be better and give us less support headaches:<br/>
<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
No namespace on &quot;{0}&quot; element. You must send a SOAP request.<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
<br/>
Or a message to the effect that a SOAP request is expected instead of a low-level failure.<br/>
<br/>
The message NO_NAMESPACE is defined in {{rt\bindings\soap\src\main\java\org\apache\cxf\binding\soap\interceptor\Messages.properties}}<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
