                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Tomcat web server
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi ,<br/>
<br/>
 I apologize, if I have chosen wrong issue type.<br/>
<br/>
 I use contract first web service where xsd is defined in external file. <br/>
 [by default, nillable is false if we haven&#39;t mentioned for elements in xsd]<br/>
<br/>
 I used jaxws-maven-plugin to import java classes from wsdl. I noticed that nillable attribute is missing for @XmlElement(required = true) [java data type string]. I assume, its the default behaviour, so Jaxb will treat those element as nillable false.<br/>
<br/>
 But when the user sends empty tag, my web service accepts that value. <br/>
<br/>
 Without touching the xsd (setting minLength for the string), is there a easy way to do non empty string validation?<br/>
<br/>
 <br/>
<br/>
 
  </td>
