                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I downloaded apache-cxf-2.5.0.zip many moons ago. It had cxf-utils.js available in the &#39;etc&#39; directory as advertised on http://cxf.apache.org/docs/javascript-client-code.html. Version 2.5.0 is no longer available from http://cxf.apache.org/download.html. Version 2.5.6 is the latest 2.5.x release available for download. Version 2.5.6 does not have etc/cxf-utils.js. I need cxf-utils.js. I found cxf-utils.js in the source code distribution but cxf-utils.js should be available in the binary distribution.<br/>
<br/>
I think cxf-utils.js is missing from the 2.6.x and 2.7.x releases as well.
  </td>
