    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 04/Dec/12 18:21 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 19/Dec/12 14:38 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 05/Dec/12 13:30 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.7            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.6.4,                     2.7.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS Security            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When using pre-authorized tokens I need the requested scope to be able to create the token.<br/>
<br/>
Please change the OAuthDataProvider interface to include:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
ServerAccessToken getPreauthorizedToken(Client client,<br/>
                                        UserSubject subject,<br/>
                                        String grantType, <br/>
                                        List&lt;String&gt; requestedScope)<br/>
    throws OAuthServiceException;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
And change RedirectionBasedGrantService.java and AbstractGrantHandler.java to pass the requestedScope variable in to getPreauthorizedToken.<br/>
<br/>
Thanks.
  </td>
