                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      There are two issues in the current exception handling of WS-RM.<br/>
<br/>
1. When the exception is constructed, it sets the subCode attribute even for the SOAP 1.1 binding<br/>
2. The exception is simply thrown in the inbound chain and the fault message is not returned to the caller if the call is oneway.<br/>

  </td>
