                <tr id="issuerow12629475" rel="12629475" data-issuekey="CXF-4784" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-4784" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-4784">CXF-4784</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                enhance CXF to follow jaxws spec 3.6.2.3 when using RI or Axis2 client
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Freeman Fang
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Bin Zhu
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Bin Zhu
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 28/Jan/13 05:10 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 28/Feb/13 17:27 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Jan/13 06:30 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.6.2,                     2.6.5,                     2.7.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.5.9,                     2.6.6,                     2.7.3,                     3.0.0-milestone1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-WS Runtime            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The content of the Outbound SOAP message in RPC/literal web service in current CXF is like below:<br/>
&lt;soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot;&gt;<br/>
&lt;soap:Body&gt;<br/>
&lt;ns1:returnNullResponse xmlns:ns1=&quot;http://serverrpc.testdata.soapbinding.annotations/&quot;&gt;<br/>
&lt;soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
&lt;faultcode&gt;soap:Server&lt;/faultcode&gt;<br/>
&lt;faultstring&gt;Cannot write part return. RPC/Literal parts cannot be null. (WS-I BP R2211)&lt;/faultstring&gt;<br/>
&lt;/soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
&lt;/ns1:returnNullResponse&gt;<br/>
&lt;/soap:Body&gt;<br/>
&lt;/soap:Envelope&gt;<br/>
If we use RI/Axis2 client, then it will not catch the WebServiceException. The reason is that CXF wrapped the Fault in the common response element.<br/>
With this fix, the SOAP message in this scenario will be like below, which will catch the WebServiceException using RI/Axis2 client.<br/>
&lt;soap:Envelope xmlns:soap=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot;&gt;<br/>
   &lt;soap:Body&gt;<br/>
      &lt;soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
         &lt;faultcode&gt;soap:Server&lt;/faultcode&gt;<br/>
         &lt;faultstring&gt;Cannot write part return. RPC/Literal parts cannot be null. (WS-I BP R2211)&lt;/faultstring&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/soap:Fault&gt;<br/>
   &lt;/soap:Body&gt;<br/>
&lt;/soap:Envelope&gt;
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
