</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      All
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      It would be really handy to have a wrapped lists not implement a wrapper class, but instead just generate List&lt;T&gt; references (classes, and method signatures in services.)<br/>
<br/>
Similar to the xew xjc plugin: https://github.com/dmak/jaxb-xew-plugin<br/>
<br/>
&lt;CarList&gt;<br/>
   &lt;Car type=&quot;import&quot; engine=&quot;v6&quot;/&gt;<br/>
   &lt;Car type=&quot;domestic&quot; engine=&quot;v8&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;/CarList&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Currently.. <br/>
<br/>
List&lt;Car&gt; cars = CarList.getCar()... <br/>
                   ^-- No need for the &quot;CarList.class&quot;<br/>
<br/>
Thanks!<br/>
Matt
