                <tr id="issuerow12637897" rel="12637897" data-issuekey="CXF-4906" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-4906" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-4906">CXF-4906</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Http Headers should ignore the case for &quot;User-Agent&quot;
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Willem Jiang
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Willem Jiang
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Willem Jiang
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 20/Mar/13 06:07 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 09/Apr/13 15:15 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 20/Mar/13 06:57 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.5.9,                     2.6.6,                     2.7.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.7.4,                     2.6.7,                     3.0.0-milestone1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Headers is using below code to setup the User-Agent header.<br/>
{code}<br/>
if (!connection.getRequestProperties().containsKey(&quot;User-Agent&quot;)) {<br/>
connection.addRequestProperty(&quot;User-Agent&quot;, Version.getCompleteVersionString());<br/>
}<br/>
{code}<br/>
As you know, http header should ignore the case, the fix should help CXF avoid sending more than one &quot;User-Agent&quot; header.
  </td>
