                <tr id="issuerow12639334" rel="12639334" data-issuekey="CXF-4930" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-4930" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-4930">CXF-4930</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Adding a http header using interceptors fails with messages above 4KB
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Not A Problem
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Michel Lampo
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Michel Lampo
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Mar/13 14:55 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 09/Apr/13 15:19 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 27/Mar/13 15:41 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.7.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-WS Runtime,                     OSGi            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Both windows and Linux, Java 1.6, server is a Tomcat 7, the client is a RAP/RCP 3.8.1 osgi application
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I have created an in-interceptor on the client to read the http-headers and save the JSESSIONID cookie value.<br/>
<br/>
Using an out-interceptor on the client I then put this value in each request. This way we know which user did the request.<br/>
<br/>
This works fine if the http request are smaller then 4KB. (Sniffed with wireshark) If it&#39;s larger, the http header with the JSESSIONID is not added. Using breakpoints I&#39;ve been able to step through the interceptor code and it works without a problem but the header is just not there.
  </td>
