                <tr id="issuerow12648198" rel="12648198" data-issuekey="CXF-5022" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5022" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5022">CXF-5022</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Multiple JAX-RS services will start on the same address, but &quot;last one&quot; wins
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 17/May/13 16:00 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 14/Aug/13 15:49 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 17/May/13 18:09 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.7.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.6.9,                     2.7.6            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
If you start multiple JAX-RS services on the same address (for example, in separate OSGi bundles), there is no warning or anything that the last one is the only one that will then work.   This should behave like SOAP where an exception is thrown if you try to start a service on an address that is already being used.
  </td>
