                <tr id="issuerow12649316" rel="12649316" data-issuekey="CXF-5038" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5038" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5038">CXF-5038</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                More flexible QueryParams
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Implemented
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Vincent Tremblay
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Vincent Tremblay
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 24/May/13 12:43 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 10/Apr/17 19:06 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 24/May/13 13:59 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      It would be useful to be able to handle how a beans are traduced into QueryParams.<br/>
<br/>
I can see something like a ParametersWriter&lt;T&gt; and a ParametersReader&lt;T&gt; to achieve this goal.<br/>
<br/>
Ex.<br/>
<br/>
Let&#39;s say that you have the following method:<br/>
<br/>
@GET<br/>
@Path(&quot;/resource&quot;)<br/>
public void doSomething(@QueryParam ComplexObject);<br/>
<br/>
You could declare a ParametersWriter that can handle the creation of the parameters:<br/>
<br/>
public class ParametersWriter&lt;ComplexObject&gt; {<br/>
    <br/>
    writeParameters(ComplexObject object, Map&lt;String, List&lt;Object&gt;&gt; params) {<br/>
<br/>
         params.put(&quot;filter&quot;, Arrays.asList(...,...));<br/>
         params.put(&quot;query&quot;, Arrays.asList(...));<br/>
<br/>
    }<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
Then, on the server side, you could have a ParametersReader&lt;ComplexObject&gt; that can rebuild the object from the request&#39;s parameters.<br/>

  </td>
